      "title": "How to read this workflow",
      "properties": {
        "widget_ue_connectable": {}
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "# 01 \u00b7 SDXL img2img \u2014 process capture\n\nThis is the single-model graph, extended so you can see how the image is made.\n\n- **KSampler (capture process)** runs the normal SDXL img2img sampling (DreamShaper XL, 30 steps, denoise 0.75) and sends decoded frames to the UI while it works.\n- **final image** is the full-resolution result, also saved to `outputs/session/<run_id>/final.png`.\n- **denoising process (GIF)** is the saved animation, `outputs/session/<run_id>/process.gif`; it plays automatically in the node and in Queue History once the prompt finishes.\n- Every run appends to `outputs/session/session.html` \u2014 open it to see all previous generations from this session with their GIFs and final images.\n\nThe GIF uses every 2nd sampling step at 512 px, 8 fps. Change `frame_stride`, `max_side` or `fps` on the sampler node to taste. To use NoobAI instead, change the checkpoint in the loader; the capture works the same way."
      ]
    }
